2165
01:29:17.184 --> 01:29:21.434
And he could see Paul tell Ringo what riff he wants

2166
01:29:23.063 --> 01:29:24.854
and talk to George about the mechanics

2167
01:29:24.854 --> 01:29:28.021
of what he was looking for for a particular song.

2168
01:29:28.021 --> 01:29:30.176
I think it's Get Back or one of the songs.

2169
01:29:30.176 --> 01:29:34.033
And to be able to see Paul just rock in his chair

2170
01:29:34.033 --> 01:29:37.175
and actually create Get Back in such a riveting way.

2171
01:29:37.175 --> 01:29:38.943
You thought Ringo looked bored.

2172
01:29:38.943 --> 01:29:41.305
I thought Ringo got it and was hooked.

2173
01:29:41.305 --> 01:29:43.856
Like I felt him getting it,

2174
01:29:43.856 --> 01:29:45.874
whereas George seemed like he was yawning.

2175
01:29:45.874 --> 01:29:46.707
(indistinct chatter)

2176
01:29:46.707 --> 01:29:48.461
Yeah, I mean, I tweeted that.

2177
01:29:48.461 --> 01:29:51.174
There's one scene that's just unbelievable

2178
01:29:51.174 --> 01:29:53.091
where Paul is literally

2179
01:29:54.544 --> 01:29:57.115
creating Get Back (indistinct) whole cloth in real time.

2180
01:29:57.115 --> 01:29:59.673
Like you can see it percolating up in his consciousness

2181
01:29:59.673 --> 01:30:02.622
and playing it and you hear the kind of...

2182
01:30:02.622 --> 01:30:04.186
You see where it's going.

2183
01:30:04.186 --> 01:30:05.903
And there's George yawning.

2184
01:30:05.903 --> 01:30:08.035
And look, it's not a slight on George.

2185
01:30:08.035 --> 01:30:09.834
Like maybe they'd been there like eight hours

2186
01:30:09.834 --> 01:30:12.173
and he'd been doing that for three hours, who knows?

2187
01:30:12.173 --> 01:30:13.526
To me Ringo look bored too

2188
01:30:13.526 --> 01:30:16.687
but the idea that you're a fly on the wall

2189
01:30:16.687 --> 01:30:21.687
and you're seeing the inception of these phenomenal songs

2190
01:30:21.734 --> 01:30:26.734
just percolate up out of nothing is really miraculous.

2191
01:30:26.996 --> 01:30:28.744
The same thing happens with Let It Be.

2192
01:30:28.744 --> 01:30:29.577
Yeah.

2193
01:30:29.577 --> 01:30:31.275
Paul is like at the piano

2194
01:30:31.275 --> 01:30:32.494
and he starting to play let it...

2195
01:30:32.494 --> 01:30:33.884
He's working it out.

2196
01:30:33.884 --> 01:30:35.887
And everybody around him

2197
01:30:35.887 --> 01:30:37.886
is like talking about a bunch of bullshit.

2198
01:30:37.886 --> 01:30:39.069
They're like distract...

2199
01:30:39.069 --> 01:30:41.249
They're doing other stuff and you're like,

2200
01:30:41.249 --> 01:30:43.678
"Do you realize what's happening right now?"

2201
01:30:43.678 --> 01:30:46.813
How incredible that there were cameras rolling

2202
01:30:46.813 --> 01:30:48.192
at that very moment.

2203
01:30:48.192 --> 01:30:49.863
It seems like he starts with a melody

2204
01:30:49.863 --> 01:30:51.703
and maybe a hook in the vocals.

2205
01:30:51.703 --> 01:30:52.943
And then he builds the rest of it.

2206
01:30:52.943 --> 01:30:54.614
He is not worried about the words as much-

2207
01:30:54.614 --> 01:30:55.452
We have the lyrics,

2208
01:30:55.452 --> 01:30:57.514
like yeah they just come through a lot of the lyrics

2209
01:30:57.514 --> 01:31:00.004
and they kind of figure it out in a group setting.

2210
01:31:00.004 --> 01:31:01.604
Yeah, and then John-

2211
01:31:01.604 --> 01:31:03.763
And they're very cavalier about the lyrics at times too.

2212
01:31:03.763 --> 01:31:05.824
John is much more the words guy it seems to me.

2213
01:31:05.824 --> 01:31:07.785
Although then Paul edits him a little bit like,

2214
01:31:07.785 --> 01:31:10.002
"This is like too on the nose or too corny."

2215
01:31:10.002 --> 01:31:11.752
And that stuff to me,

2216
01:31:13.713 --> 01:31:15.645
to be able to see the creative process

2217
01:31:15.645 --> 01:31:19.713
of one of the greatest partnerships in all of creation,

2218
01:31:19.713 --> 01:31:22.604
certainly in all of, I guess,

2219
01:31:22.604 --> 01:31:25.934
Western popular culture to be able

2220
01:31:25.934 --> 01:31:28.581
to witness that is spectacular.

2221
01:31:28.581 --> 01:31:29.934
The reason that you're saying,

2222
01:31:29.934 --> 01:31:30.767
"And it's not for everybody."

2223
01:31:30.767 --> 01:31:32.645
Is that some people just wanna listen to the hits

2224
01:31:32.645 --> 01:31:34.804
and they don't really need to get into the minutia.

2225
01:31:34.804 --> 01:31:36.952
So for them, and that's certainly the case

2226
01:31:36.952 --> 01:31:37.952
of people I watched it with,

2227
01:31:37.952 --> 01:31:39.963
they thought it was a little bit too slow

2228
01:31:39.963 --> 01:31:42.353
and that it was a little too aimless.

2229
01:31:42.353 --> 01:31:44.243
And it was a little too, a little too-

2230
01:31:44.243 --> 01:31:48.954
I would sit through all 56 hours of it unedited.

2231
01:31:48.954 --> 01:31:53.371
Because I think it's such a rare and precious glimpse

2232
01:31:54.593 --> 01:31:59.426
into not only genius, but the creative process in general.

2233
01:32:00.374 --> 01:32:03.753
If you have any interest in how creativity operates,

2234
01:32:03.753 --> 01:32:05.884
especially in a group setting.

2235
01:32:05.884 --> 01:32:08.191
Whether you're a musician or a writer or a screenwriter

2236
01:32:08.191 --> 01:32:09.634
or a TV writer.

2237
01:32:09.634 --> 01:32:12.031
Anybody who's trying to birth something unique

2238
01:32:12.031 --> 01:32:13.233
and creative into the world.

2239
01:32:13.233 --> 01:32:14.953
And it has to do it with other people

2240
01:32:14.953 --> 01:32:19.953
to observe how some of the greatest songs ever crafted

2241
01:32:20.266 --> 01:32:23.665
came together with a group of people

2242
01:32:23.665 --> 01:32:26.434
who were having issues at the time.

2243
01:32:26.434 --> 01:32:29.434
And I think it also is a litmus test

2244
01:32:31.506 --> 01:32:33.923
regarding how attuned you are

2245
01:32:35.094 --> 01:32:38.124
to what those creative processes look like.

2246
01:32:38.124 --> 01:32:40.675
Have you had experience with them or not.

2247
01:32:40.675 --> 01:32:42.605
People who have not been in bands

2248
01:32:42.605 --> 01:32:46.433
or haven't been in TV writing rooms or things like that,

2249
01:32:46.433 --> 01:32:48.805
could observe what was happening with the band

2250
01:32:48.805 --> 01:32:50.779
and say, "Oh, you could tell, they're not getting along.

2251
01:32:50.779 --> 01:32:52.953
You could tell this band's about to break up.

2252
01:32:52.953 --> 01:32:55.063
This is all falling apart."

2253
01:32:55.063 --> 01:32:56.591
But if you've been in a band

2254
01:32:56.591 --> 01:33:01.111
or you have tried to collaborate on something creative.

2255
01:33:01.111 --> 01:33:03.741
I saw that and I thought they have a really...

2256
01:33:03.741 --> 01:33:04.862
Cause there's this narrative like,

2257
01:33:04.862 --> 01:33:06.229
"Oh, they all hated each other.

2258
01:33:06.229 --> 01:33:08.521
And they were breaking up and they couldn't communicate."

2259
01:33:08.521 --> 01:33:10.974
I saw very healthy communication.

2260
01:33:10.974 --> 01:33:12.402
They would disagree about things.

2261
01:33:12.402 --> 01:33:13.253
They didn't seem to hate each other.

2262
01:33:13.253 --> 01:33:16.402
They always treated each other with respect and grace.

2263
01:33:16.402 --> 01:33:19.322
They maintained their equanimity at all times.

2264
01:33:19.322 --> 01:33:22.924
There was always levity and comedy.

2265
01:33:22.924 --> 01:33:24.671
Like they're always cracking jokes.

2266
01:33:24.671 --> 01:33:26.082
They had their difficult moments.

2267
01:33:26.082 --> 01:33:28.122
And I don't wanna spoil that for people who haven't seen it

2268
01:33:28.122 --> 01:33:30.821
because things actually go down like shit hits the fan

2269
01:33:30.821 --> 01:33:31.654
and stuff like that.

2270
01:33:31.654 --> 01:33:34.896
But overall, I saw a group of people

2271
01:33:34.896 --> 01:33:39.656
who really love each other and were trying to do something.

2272
01:33:39.656 --> 01:33:41.833
Yeah, George did seem a little pissy.

2273
01:33:41.833 --> 01:33:42.675
I will say that.

2274
01:33:42.675 --> 01:33:44.836
Well, we'll let people watch it

2275
01:33:44.836 --> 01:33:46.725
and form their own opinion about that.

2276
01:33:46.725 --> 01:33:48.865
I know you have issues with George.

2277
01:33:48.865 --> 01:33:50.264
I always love.

2278
01:33:50.264 --> 01:33:53.472
(indistinct chatter)

2279
01:33:53.472 --> 01:33:54.847
What's the other one I love?

2280
01:33:54.847 --> 01:33:56.954
Listen, there's something very special

2281
01:33:56.954 --> 01:33:58.787
between Paul and John.

2282
01:34:01.906 --> 01:34:05.906
That made it very difficult for someone like George,

2283
01:34:05.906 --> 01:34:09.536
who is extremely gifted to have his voice being heard.

2284
01:34:09.536 --> 01:34:11.565
And that's gotta be really challenging.

2285
01:34:11.565 --> 01:34:15.315
And Paul and John, admit as much in the film.

2286
01:34:16.909 --> 01:34:18.256
And so that's kind of where things start

2287
01:34:18.256 --> 01:34:19.817
