3149
02:08:41.378 --> 02:08:44.711
that George Washington was Brian Epstein

3150
02:08:50.171 --> 02:08:52.921
and Ben Franklin was John Lennon.

3151
02:08:55.879 --> 02:08:57.841
Why am I spacing on the most-

3152
02:08:57.841 --> 02:08:58.979
(indistinct chatter)

3153
02:08:58.979 --> 02:08:59.812
Thomas Jefferson.

3154
02:08:59.812 --> 02:09:02.662
Thomas Jefferson was Paul.

3155
02:09:02.662 --> 02:09:05.209
Yeah, very industrious and productive.

3156
02:09:05.209 --> 02:09:06.600
Who's George?

3157
02:09:06.600 --> 02:09:07.692
Who's Ringo?

3158
02:09:07.692 --> 02:09:08.631
John Quincy Adams.

3159
02:09:08.631 --> 02:09:11.912
(both laughing)

3160
02:09:11.912 --> 02:09:12.759
How do we layer that-

3161
02:09:12.759 --> 02:09:15.842
(indistinct chatter)

3162
02:09:16.775 --> 02:09:17.608
Maybe.

3163
02:09:19.443 --> 02:09:20.802
Yeah, that's an interesting question.

3164
02:09:20.802 --> 02:09:22.633
I mean, I can't read the minds of the founding fathers.

3165
02:09:22.633 --> 02:09:24.682
I have no idea what they were thinking about.

3166
02:09:24.682 --> 02:09:27.300
My interpretation though, is that

3167
02:09:27.300 --> 02:09:30.743
it's about the liberty of the pursuit.

3168
02:09:30.743 --> 02:09:32.322
So whether it's the pursuit of...

3169
02:09:32.322 --> 02:09:36.284
I don't know whether they ever expanded upon

3170
02:09:36.284 --> 02:09:39.311
how they define happiness or whether happiness

3171
02:09:39.311 --> 02:09:41.142
can only be found through the pursuit.

3172
02:09:41.142 --> 02:09:44.472
I'm not sure that they really thought that through

3173
02:09:44.472 --> 02:09:46.801
all that (indistinct), I don't know.

3174
02:09:46.801 --> 02:09:50.551
But for me, it's about the liberty to pursue.

3175
02:09:52.709 --> 02:09:55.709
And I don't think it's good practice

3176
02:09:59.201 --> 02:10:03.784
to be orienting your life around this aim of happiness.

3177
02:10:05.178 --> 02:10:08.931
I mean, happiness is a choice that we have in every moment.

3178
02:10:08.931 --> 02:10:10.700
We can choose to be happy.

3179
02:10:10.700 --> 02:10:12.460
We can choose to not be happy.

3180
02:10:12.460 --> 02:10:17.211
And in my opinion, the pursuit should be focused on meaning

3181
02:10:17.211 --> 02:10:20.351
and fulfillment and giving back service.

3182
02:10:20.351 --> 02:10:21.749
Things like that.

3183
02:10:21.749 --> 02:10:25.501
And I think happiness is a by-product of doing other things.

3184
02:10:25.501 --> 02:10:29.071
Not an end to be pursued in it of itself.

3185
02:10:29.071 --> 02:10:33.251
And personally, I mean, the things that make me happy

3186
02:10:33.251 --> 02:10:36.882
are really kind of a temporal states.

3187
02:10:36.882 --> 02:10:39.111
"Oh, I like jumping in the ocean.

3188
02:10:39.111 --> 02:10:40.521
You know, something of that...

3189
02:10:40.521 --> 02:10:41.354
That makes me happy.

3190
02:10:41.354 --> 02:10:44.920
But my life isn't in pursuit of jumping in the ocean.

3191
02:10:44.920 --> 02:10:49.837
It's a fleeting thing that I enjoy that gives me happiness.

3192
02:10:50.978 --> 02:10:54.311
But more broadly, the things that create

3193
02:10:56.046 --> 02:10:58.998
an extended sense of happiness in my life

3194
02:10:58.998 --> 02:11:02.031
are not the things that were kind of forced fed

3195
02:11:02.031 --> 02:11:03.680
in our culture.

3196
02:11:03.680 --> 02:11:08.680
Like luxury and convenience and what your bank account says

3197
02:11:08.730 --> 02:11:09.563
and all of that.

3198
02:11:09.563 --> 02:11:10.924
They're really the result of strain

3199
02:11:10.924 --> 02:11:14.155
or getting out of my comfort zone, tackling hard things.

3200
02:11:14.155 --> 02:11:17.636
Trying to find a way to give back, pushing my own limits.

3201
02:11:17.636 --> 02:11:20.025
And as an American, I'm very grateful

3202
02:11:20.025 --> 02:11:23.863
to have the Liberty to explore these things.

3203
02:11:23.863 --> 02:11:26.927
Which in turn ultimately lead to

3204
02:11:26.927 --> 02:11:28.614
a greater sense of happiness.

3205
02:11:28.614 --> 02:11:30.294
But I don't think about my life in the context

3206
02:11:30.294 --> 02:11:32.596
of happiness every day.

3207
02:11:32.596 --> 02:11:34.753
That's exactly how it works for me.

3208
02:11:34.753 --> 02:11:37.286
I don't think that's how it works for anybody.

3209
02:11:37.286 --> 02:11:38.894
I think that's what Kendall's getting at.

3210
02:11:38.894 --> 02:11:40.288
I think he wants you to speak to...

3211
02:11:40.288 --> 02:11:42.276
I mean, I think that he's kind of teeing it up in that way.

3212
02:11:42.276 --> 02:11:45.515
I think he agrees that it's about the pursuit

3213
02:11:45.515 --> 02:11:48.787
of some meaning or about the...

3214
02:11:48.787 --> 02:11:51.584
But I think you're also getting at what they're...

3215
02:11:51.584 --> 02:11:54.447
They're not trying to define pursuit or happiness.

3216
02:11:54.447 --> 02:11:56.927
So while I agree with you, and I think Kendall

3217
02:11:56.927 --> 02:11:58.496
is saying the same thing,

3218
02:11:58.496 --> 02:12:00.166
and that's why he wants us to speak to this.

3219
02:12:00.166 --> 02:12:02.938
The idea isn't to happiness as this goal,

3220
02:12:02.938 --> 02:12:05.568
but happiness can come in the pursuit.

3221
02:12:05.568 --> 02:12:07.386
I don't disagree with that.

3222
02:12:07.386 --> 02:12:12.386
But I think what they were getting at was more creating

3223
02:12:12.476 --> 02:12:16.319
the environment so that everyone felt the feel

3224
02:12:16.319 --> 02:12:19.522
like they can pursue whatever they want.

3225
02:12:19.522 --> 02:12:21.505
And so obviously they didn't...

3226
02:12:21.505 --> 02:12:22.838
That's the liberty...

3227
02:12:22.838 --> 02:12:23.850
That's the liberty piece.

3228
02:12:23.850 --> 02:12:25.318
But in their mind they created it

3229
02:12:25.318 --> 02:12:28.433
in their narrow construct of what they thought

3230
02:12:28.433 --> 02:12:32.122
was appropriate and good for the white male.

3231
02:12:32.122 --> 02:12:36.451
But that was that time, and that's what they did.

3232
02:12:36.451 --> 02:12:38.101
But I think if you look back they weren't...

3233
02:12:38.101 --> 02:12:39.433
They weren't actually creating that,

3234
02:12:39.433 --> 02:12:40.266
after they thought they were

3235
02:12:40.266 --> 02:12:42.888
or they tried to frame it that way.

3236
02:12:42.888 --> 02:12:46.295
But because when you look at studies.

3237
02:12:46.295 --> 02:12:50.208
If you're in a country where it's harder to get a loan,

3238
02:12:50.208 --> 02:12:51.357
you can't start a business.

3239
02:12:51.357 --> 02:12:54.329
If you look at Venezuela or Cuba or these places,

3240
02:12:54.329 --> 02:12:56.489
there's a lot of unhappiness because the structures

3241
02:12:56.489 --> 02:12:58.017
of that society, aren't allowing

3242
02:12:58.017 --> 02:13:00.808
for the pursuit of anything really.

3243
02:13:00.808 --> 02:13:03.167
And so I think the idea was let's create a place

3244
02:13:03.167 --> 02:13:04.642
where the crown is not getting in the way,

3245
02:13:04.642 --> 02:13:07.468
where taxes are low, where you can really just go out

3246
02:13:07.468 --> 02:13:08.301
and do what you...

3247
02:13:08.301 --> 02:13:10.218
And equitable access.

3248
02:13:11.468 --> 02:13:13.030
Right, equitable access,

3249
02:13:13.030 --> 02:13:15.889
which is the thing that we would like to expand.

3250
02:13:15.889 --> 02:13:19.508
Because obviously it was imperfect then, it's imperfect now.

3251
02:13:19.508 --> 02:13:22.750
But that idea of that democracy

3252
02:13:22.750 --> 02:13:24.765
is obviously something special

3253
02:13:24.765 --> 02:13:27.357
because it has been replicated in many places.

3254
02:13:27.357 --> 02:13:30.242
And so I think it was creating the conditions

3255
02:13:30.242 --> 02:13:33.048
